- Add actionable suggested next steps to ticket headers, with a primary control for the first actionable step and remaining suggestions available through an overflow menu. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operated command palette available across pages, with navigation entries from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Add optimistic status updates to the board and ticket detail views, reconciling successful changes and restoring prior state when a transition is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace ticket status and assignee dialogs with inline `MudMenu` popovers that apply changes in place. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges with hover and keyboard-focus previews to assistant answers, retaining a numbered sources list for citations that are not anchored. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster to each chat system prompt and instruct the assistant to use only the listed names when assigning tickets. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `AgentLoop` to call `check_grounding` once after retrieval when no grounding check has run, using `tool_choice` to enforce the check. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Add shared design tokens for colors, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors, and use them across the frontend stylesheets; change `KpiCard.Accent` to the `KpiAccent` enum. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

